The Java idiom: when you catch `InterruptedException` and don't re-throw it as-is, you must call `Thread.currentThread().interrupt()` to preserve the signal for upstream code. Currently the `ConnectException` propagates but the interrupt flag is cleared,
so any subsequent blocking call on this thread doesn't know it was interrupted.
 
